course: dictionary
lesson: 13229
title: One word, three meanings: gassing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to choose the right one. «Stop gassing and tidy your room!» Here gassing means chatting for a long time about things that do not matter. It is old-fashioned English, and the words around it show that someone is being told off.
explain: The second meaning is a serious one. Poison gas was used to harm soldiers in the First World War, and in the Holocaust the Nazis murdered millions of people in gas chambers. When you read about gassing in history, the words around it will tell you this is the meaning, and it is a sad part of history.
explain: The third meaning is everyday American talk. «Dad stopped at the garage for gassing up the car» means filling the car with petrol. Always read the sentence again and try your meaning in place of the word to check it fits.
fact: Gassing is a verb: gas, gases, gassed, gassing. It can also be a noun, gassings.
fact: Gassing can mean chatting for a long time about small things, and it can also mean boasting.
fact: Gassing can mean poisoning or killing with gas. This is a serious history word.
fact: In America, gassing up means filling a car with petrol.
fact: Use the context to choose the right meaning, then check by putting your meaning into the sentence.
exercise: «Stop gassing and help me tidy up!» What does gassing mean here? | Filling a car with petrol | Poisoning with gas | *Chatting for a long time about things that do not matter | Singing loudly
exercise: «The soldiers were gassed in the war.» What does gassed mean here? | Chatted for hours | *Poisoned or killed with gas | Cheered loudly | Filled with petrol
exercise: «Dad stopped at the station for gassing up the car.» Which meaning fits? | Washing the car | Poisoning the air | *Filling the car with petrol | Telling a long, boring story
test: «The two aunties were gassing about their gardens for an hour.» What does gassing mean? | Shouting at the neighbours | Filling a car with petrol | Poisoning with gas | *Talking for a long time about not very important things
test: Which meaning of gassing is a serious history word? | Boasting at school | Chatting about nothing | *Poisoning or killing with poison gas | Filling a car with petrol
exam: How can you tell which meaning of gassing is right in «Stop gassing and tidy up!»? | Always pick the longest meaning | *Read the clues: someone is told to stop and do a job, so gassing means chatting | Look only at the first letter | Count the letters in the word
